Level 1: Data Inspection (Know Your Data)

These are the first methods you use after loading a dataset.

Method	Purpose	Why use it?
head()	Show first rows	Quickly inspect data
tail()	Show last rows	Check the end of the dataset
sample()	Random rows	Inspect random records
shape	Number of rows and columns	Understand dataset size
info()	Column types and missing values	Most important first inspection
describe()	Statistical summary	Understand numeric columns
columns	Column names	Useful for selecting and renaming
index	Row labels	Understand indexing
dtypes	Data type of each column	Know how Pandas interprets data
memory_usage()	Memory consumed	Optimize large datasets

.......................................................................................

Level 2: Selecting Data

Probably the most used operations in Pandas.

Method	Purpose
[]	Select columns
.loc[]	Label-based selection
.iloc[]	Position-based selection
.at[]	Fast access to one value
.iat[]	Fast integer-position access
.query()	SQL-like filtering
.filter()	Select columns by name or pattern
..........................................................................................

Level 3: Cleaning Data

This is where analysts spend most of their time.

Method	Purpose
isnull()	Find missing values
notnull()	Opposite of isnull()
dropna()	Remove missing rows
fillna()	Replace missing values
replace()	Replace specific values
map()	Convert values using a dictionary
astype()	Change data type
rename()	Rename columns
drop()	Remove rows or columns
duplicated()	Find duplicates
drop_duplicates()	Remove duplicates
clip()	Limit values to a range

